652 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 271 0 R/E(OpenText Forensic TX2 Imager is a high-performance standalone forensic imaging hardware solution designed for fast and defensible acquisition of digital evidence. It supports PCIe, SATA, USB, and\204through adapters\204SAS, IDE, and FireWire media, along with Apple and Android mobile backup acquisition. Key features include up to 5\327 faster acquisition and verification, concurrent imaging and verification, parallel/tree hashing, hardware write-protection workflows, PCIe hot-swap, MFA security, gallery-based triage, and multiple simultaneous imaging jobs. It is suitable for both forensic laboratories and field evidence acquisition. )/Pg 40 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

653 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 271 0 R/T(FORENSIC TD4 DUPLICATOR)/E(FORENSIC TD4 DUPLICATOR)/Pg 40 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

654 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 271 0 R/E(OpenText Forensic TD4 Duplicator is a portable forensic hardware solution designed for rapid field triage, disk acquisition, duplication, and media management. It supports SATA, SAS, PCIe, and USB drives, with PCIe hot-swapping, targeted logical imaging, disk-to-disk or disk-to-file duplication, and up to five destination copies per job. It also provides MD5, SHA-1, and SHA-256 hashing, file-system awareness, detailed logs, touchscreen workflows, and secure media wiping and formatting, helping investigators acquire and manage digital evidence efficiently while maintaining evidence integrity.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

655 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 271 0 R/T(FORENSIC BRIDGES WRITE BLOCKER)/E(FORENSIC BRIDGES WRITE BLOCKER)/Pg 40 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

656 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 271 0 R/E(OpenText Forensic Bridges are professional hardware write blockers designed to prevent write access to suspect storage media during forensic acquisition, providing read-only access and helping preserve evidence integrity and chain of custody. They support a broad range of interfaces, including SATA, SAS, PCIe, USB 3.0, IDE, and FireWire, with transfer speeds of up to 5 GB/s via USB 3.0 host connection. Available in portable and drive-bay formats, they are suitable for both field operations and forensic laboratories, providing secure, reliable, and forensically sound evidence acquisition.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

