668 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(RapiDFIR by iinefu is an AI-driven Digital Forensics and Incident Response \(DFIR\) platform designed for SOCs, MSSPs, DFIR teams, and law enforcement to rapidly investigate cyber incidents. It enables remote evidence collection from distributed endpoints, automated forensic artifact analysis, real-time dashboards, centralized case management, AI-assisted investigations, one-click forensic reporting, and EDR/SOAR integration. With support for 100+ forensic artifacts, RapiDFIR helps organizations detect, prioritize, and respond to cyber threats faster while reducing manual investigation time and minimizing the need for on-site forensic teams. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

669 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(ENDPOINT FORENSICS & RESPONSE)/E(ENDPOINT FORENSICS & RESPONSE)/Pg 42 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

670 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(OpenText Endpoint Forensics & Response is an enterprise-grade DFIR platform that combines deep endpoint forensics with near real-time incident response. It enables security teams to collect and analyze live endpoint evidence, investigate threats, isolate compromised systems, terminate malicious processes, remediate files, and hunt for indicators of compromise \(IoCs\) from a single platform. It supports artifact-driven triage, YARA-based IoC scanning, registry analysis, memory investigation, automated zero-trust collections, and large-scale deployments of over 1 million endpoints, making it suitable for ransomware response, insider-threat investigations, APT hunting, breach response, and compliance investigations.)/Pg 42 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

671 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(ENDPOINT INVESTIGATOR)/E(ENDPOINT INVESTIGATOR)/Pg 42 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

672 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(OpenText Endpoint Investigator is an enterprise-grade digital forensics and internal investigation platform designed for discreet, remote, and forensically sound evidence collection across laptops, desktops, servers, and mobile devices. It enables investigators to remotely search, collect, and analyze endpoint data both on and off VPN, with automated agent deployment and support for large-scale environments exceeding 1 million endpoints. It is particularly suited for cybercrime, data breach, fraud, insider-threat, HR, compliance, IP theft, and regulatory investigations, while minimizing disruption to employees. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

