endobj

888 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 295 0 R/E(Jamf Mobile Forensics is an advanced mobile threat detection, DFIR, and forensic analysis solution for iOS and Android devices, designed primarily to protect high-risk users and organizations against mercenary spyware such as Pegasus and Predator, zero-click exploits, APTs, and other sophisticated attacks. It automatically collects and analyzes system, kernel, application, crash, Wi-Fi, and security telemetry without rooting or jailbreaking the device and without collecting personal content such as messages, photos, passwords, contacts, or call data. It uses behavioral analytics, Indicators of Compromise \(IoCs\), automated rules, incident timelines, and AI-assisted analysis to identify suspicious activity and help security teams investigate and respond quickly. It supports remote DFIR, proactive threat hunting, SOC workflows, MDM deployment, and SIEM/SOAR integrations, making it particularly suitable for government, enterprise, and other high-security environments.)/Pg 64 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

889 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 295 0 R/T(JAMF PRO - ENTERPRISE)/E(JAMF PRO - ENTERPRISE)/Pg 64 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

890 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 295 0 R/E(Jamf Pro is an enterprise-grade Apple device management \(MDM\) platform used by organizations to centrally manage and secure Mac, iPhone, iPad, Apple TV, Apple Watch, and Apple Vision Pro devices. It enables IT teams to enroll devices, configure security settings, deploy and update applications, manage operating-system updates, maintain hardware/software inventory, enforce compliance policies, and remotely issue management commands. Its zero-touch deployment allows devices to be automatically configured when issued to users, while Smart Groups and policies help automate management for large device fleets. Devices are enrolled into Jamf Pro, typically through Apple Business Manager/Automated Device Enrollment or user-initiated enrollment. Once enrolled, administrators manage them remotely through the Jamf Pro web console, applying configurations, apps, restrictions, updates, and security policies.)/Pg 64 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

