929 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 299 0 R/E(Elcomsoft Distributed Password Recovery \(EDPR\) is high-performance password recovery solution designed for forensic, government, corporate, and data recovery environments. It can recover passwords and encryption keys across 300+ data formats, including Microsoft Office, PDF, ZIP/RAR, BitLocker, PGP, TrueCrypt, VeraCrypt, FileVault 2, and LUKS. EDPR uses GPU-accelerated processing with NVIDIA and AMD hardware, supports heterogeneous GPUs, and provides distributed recovery across up to 10,000 networked computers with linear scalability. It also offers centralized job management, remote deployment, and resource monitoring, making it suitable for large-scale forensic and password recovery operations.)/Pg 68 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

930 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 299 0 R/E(FORENSIC DISK DECRYPTOR)/Pg 68 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

931 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 299 0 R/E(Elcomsoft Forensic Disk Decryptor \(EFDD\) is a specialized digital forensic solution designed to access and decrypt encrypted disks, volumes, and containers protected by BitLocker, FileVault 2, PGP Disk, TrueCrypt, VeraCrypt, LUKS/LUKS2, and BestCrypt. It can extract encryption keys from RAM captures, hibernation files, and page files, as well as use recovery or escrow keys where available. Investigators can either fully decrypt encrypted evidence or mount protected volumes for real-time access. When keys are unavailable, EFDD can extract encryption metadata for GPU-accelerated password recovery using Elcomsoft Distributed Password Recovery, making it valuable for law enforcement, government agencies, and digital forensic laboratories.)/Pg 68 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

932 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 299 0 R/E(PASSWARE KIT ULTIMATE)/Pg 68 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

933 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 299 0 R/E(Passware Kit Forensic is comprehensive encrypted-evidence discovery and decryption solution designed for digital forensic investigators, law enforcement, government agencies, and corporate investigations. It automatically identifies password-protected files and encrypted disk images, supporting 420+ file types and full-disk encryption formats such as BitLocker, FileVault2, APFS, LUKS/LUKS2, PGP, TrueCrypt, and VeraCrypt. It also provides live memory analysis, GPU-accelerated password recovery, batch processing, and distributed recovery through Passware Kit Agents, making it suitable for large-scale forensic investigations and encrypted evidence examination.)/Pg 68 0 R/K[11]>>
