978 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 304 0 R/E(Anubhooti AED4000 is an automatic speech emotion detection system designed to identify anger, aggression, happiness, sadness, fear, surprise, and stress from audio segments at five-second intervals. It supports both mono and stereo audio, with capabilities for speaker diarization, noise reduction, stereo-channel separation, automatic mood profiling, and detailed emotion reporting in CSV format. The system also provides essential audio-processing functions such as recording, playback, splitting, normalization, and visualization, and can operate as a completely offline solution, making it suitable for forensic audio analysis, call-center investigations, and investigative applications.)/Pg 73 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

979 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 304 0 R/E(ASD4000 - SPEAKER DIARIZATION)/Pg 73 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

980 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 304 0 R/E(Anubhooti ASD4000 is an automatic speaker diarization solution designed to separate and identify different speakers within disputed or multi-speaker audio recordings. It can automatically determine the number of speakers using an unsupervised mode and supports dedicated 2-, 3-, and 4-speaker diarization, with manual diarization available for recordings containing more than four speakers. The system also provides Signal-to-Noise Ratio \(SNR\) measurement, gender detection, stereo-channel separation, and essential audio-processing tools, and operates offline across mono and stereo audio formats, making it useful for forensic voice analysis and law-enforcement investigations.)/Pg 73 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

981 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 304 0 R/T(AAA5000 - AUDIO AUTHENTICATION )/E(AAA5000 - AUDIO AUTHENTICATION )/Pg 73 0 R/K[9]>>
