<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 309 0 R/E(MOBILedit Dive Computer Forensics enables forensic investigators to extract and analyze data from dive computers, which can serve as a digital record of underwater activity. The solution can recover dive dates and times, depth, duration, water temperature, dive modes, decompression information, and physiological data such as heart rate. This evidence can help reconstruct underwater events, verify diving activities, assess compliance with dive protocols, and support investigations involving diving accidents, fatalities, disappearances, or disputed accounts.)/Pg 78 0 R/K[6]>>
